Regressions for upload backpressure and receive exception handling. Pause a
streaming producer until the server writes its first block, then finish a
1 MiB upload and verify the downloaded bytes. The transfer exceeds the
HTTP/2 stream window and retains all XFTP authentication and digest checks.
Check that receive deadlines and cancellation propagate, while IO errors
still become FILE_IO. No existing example or timeout is weakened.

